{
  "name": "Score inbound leads with OpenAI and route them to Google Sheets and Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        -620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "# Score inbound leads with OpenAI and route them to Google Sheets and Slack\n\n## Who's it for\nSales and marketing teams, agencies and founders who collect leads through web forms and want to spot the best ones fast.\n\n## How it works\nA webhook receives each lead and OpenAI returns a score from 0 to 100, a hot, warm or cold tier and a one-line reason. Every lead is logged to Google Sheets. Leads at or above your threshold also trigger a Slack alert. If OpenAI fails, the lead is still logged as \"unscored\", so nothing is lost.\n\n## How to set up\n1. Create a Google Sheet with a Leads tab and these headers: name, email, company, message, score, tier, reason, receivedAt.\n2. Add your OpenAI, Google Sheets and Slack credentials.\n3. Open the **Workflow Configuration** node and set your sheet ID, Slack channel, threshold and model.\n4. Send the test payload below to the test webhook URL.\n5. Activate the workflow and point your form to the production URL.\n\n## Requirements\n- n8n Cloud or self-hosted n8n\n- OpenAI API key, Google account and Slack workspace\n\n## How to customize the workflow\n- Edit the scoring prompt to match your ideal customer.\n- Swap Slack for email or Teams, or Google Sheets for a CRM.\n- Add form fields, such as budget, and include them in the prompt.\n\n## Test payload\n```json\n{\"name\": \"Jane Doe\", \"email\": \"jane@example.com\", \"company\": \"Example Inc\", \"message\": \"We need to automate onboarding for 200 staff this quarter. Budget approved.\"}\n```"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### 1. Receive and configure\nThe webhook receives the lead. Edit your settings in **Workflow Configuration**, then **Normalize Lead** keeps only the fields we need. Missing fields become empty text so later steps never break."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### 2. Score with AI\nOpenAI returns a score, tier and reason as JSON. If the call fails, the lead continues as *unscored* so it is still logged."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1140,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### 3. Log and route\nEvery lead is saved to Google Sheets. Only leads at or above your threshold send a Slack alert."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Receive Lead Form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        0,
        360
      ],
      "webhookId": "c3a1d2e4-5555-4666-8777-888899990000",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "lead-intake",
        "options": {},
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "responseMode": "onReceived"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
      "name": "Workflow Configuration",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        240,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "hotLeadThreshold",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 70
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "slackChannel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#sales-leads"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "googleSheetId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "googleSheetName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Leads"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "openAiModel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Normalize Lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        480,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "name",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.name ?? '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "email",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.email ?? '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "company",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.company ?? '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f+1234567890-+1234567890",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.message ?? '' }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Score Lead with OpenAI",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        720,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: $('Workflow Configuration').item.json.openAiModel, response_format: { type: 'json_object' }, messages: [ { role: 'system', content: 'You are a B2B lead qualification assistant. Return only JSON in this shape: {\"score\": integer 0-100, \"tier\": \"hot\" or \"warm\" or \"cold\", \"reason\": one short sentence}. Score higher for clear budget, urgency, company context and a specific need.' }, { role: 'user', content: 'Name: ' + $json.name + '\\nEmail: ' + $json.email + '\\nCompany: ' + $json.company + '\\nMessage: ' + $json.message } ] }) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "openAiApi"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "credential-id",
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Parse AI Score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        960,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "\nconst lead = $('Normalize Lead').item.json;\nlet result = { score: 0, tier: 'unscored', reason: 'AI scoring failed - review manually' };\nlet aiFailed = true;\n\ntry {\n  const content = $input.item.json.choices[0].message.content;\n  const parsed = JSON.parse(content);\n  result = {\n    score: Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(parsed.score) || 0)),\n    tier: String(parsed.tier || 'cold').toLowerCase(),\n    reason: String(parsed.reason || '')\n  };\n  aiFailed = false;\n} catch (e) {\n  // Keep the safe defaults so the lead is still logged\n}\n\nreturn { json: { ...lead, ...result, aiFailed, receivedAt: new Date().toISOString() } };\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Log Lead to Google Sheets",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        1200,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "name": "={{ $json.name }}",
            "tier": "={{ $json.tier }}",
            "email": "={{ $json.email }}",
            "score": "={{ $json.score }}",
            "reason": "={{ $json.reason }}",
            "company": "={{ $json.company }}",
            "message": "={{ $json.message }}",
            "receivedAt": "={{ $json.receivedAt }}"
          },
          "schema": [],
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": []
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "={{ $('Workflow Configuration').item.json.googleSheetName }}"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Workflow Configuration').item.json.googleSheetId }}"
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "googleSheetsOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "credential-id",
          "name": "Google Sheets account"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Is Hot Lead?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
